Here's a complete, self-contained HTML page — a little "Almanack" of 25 original limericks about Bills, set in five chapters with a live stanza tracker, meter key, and a clapping feature for the pub. All three required keywords (bill, economist, jurgen) appear in the text.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>The Bill Almanack — 25 Limericks About Bills</title>
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:ital,opsz,wght@0,9..144,400;0,9..144,600;0,9..144,700;0,9..144,900;1,9..144,500;1,9..144,600;1,9..144,700&family=Crimson+Pro:ital,wght@0,400;0,500;0,600;1,500;1,600&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:ital,wght@0,400;0,500;0,600;1,400&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<style>
:root{
  --paper:#f3e9d2;
  --paper-2:#ece0c2;
  --paper-hi:#f8f1de;
  --ink:#221c12;
  --ink-soft:rgba(34,28,18,.66);
  --ink-line:rgba(34,28,18,.4);
  --green:#1d4a35;
  --green-2:#143726;
  --gold:#b9862f;
