    <div class="catalogue-cols">

      <article class="lim rev" id="lim-1">
        <div class="lim-head"><span class="num">I</span><span class="place">The Bill of Billtown</span>
          <button class="recite" type="button" title="Recite, by highlighting, at a dignified pace">▸ Recite</button>
        </div>
        <div class="lim-rule"></div>
        <p class="poem">
          <span class="ln">There once was a Bill from Billtown,</span>
          <span class="ln">Who drained every cask of the town;</span>
          <span class="ln">The casks were quite small,</span>
          <span class="ln">But Bill drained them all,</span>
          <span class="ln">And ordered another by noon.</span>
        </p>
        <div class="note"><b>Marginalia</b>The casks were, in fact, a size smaller than stated.</div>
        <span class="stamp" aria-hidden="true">Read aloud</span>
      </article>

      <article class="lim rev" id="lim-2">
        <div class="lim-head"><span class="num">II</span><span class="place">The Bill of Billport</span>
          <button class="recite" type="button" title="Recite, by highlighting, at a dignified pace">▸ Recite</button>
        </div>
        <div class="lim-rule"></div>
        <p class="poem">
          <span class="ln">There was a young Bill from Billport,</span>
          <span class="ln">Who played polka on public transport;</span>
          <span class="ln">The bus was not long,</span>
          <span class="ln">But he jigged along,</span>
          <span class="ln">And the driver said, “Mate, that’s no sport.”</span>
        </p>
        <div class="note"><b>Marginalia</b>The bus company denies all responsibility, and most injuries.</div>
        <span class="stamp" aria-hidden="true">Read aloud</span>
      </article>

      <article class="lim rev" id="lim-3">
        <div class="lim-head"><span class="num">III</span><span class="place">The Economist of the Markets</span>
          <button class="recite" type="button" title="Recite, by highlighting, at a dignified pace">▸ Recite</button>
        </div>
        <div class="lim-rule"></div>
        <p class="poem">
          <span class="ln">There was an economist, Bill,</span>
          <span class="ln">Who charted the markets with skill;</span>
          <span class="ln">He forecasted rain,</span>
          <span class="ln">He forecasted gain,</span>
          <span class="ln">But he never could read his own bill.</span>
        </p>
        <div class="note"><b>Marginalia</b>Forecasts: accurate. Invoices: regrettably, unread.</div>
        <span class="stamp" aria-hidden="true">Read aloud</span>
      </article>

      <article class="lim rev" id="lim-4">
        <div class="lim-head"><span class="num">IV</span><span class="place">The Bill of Billbrook</span>
          <button class="recite" type="button" title="Recite, by highlighting, at a dignified pace">▸ Recite</button>
        </div>
        <div class="lim-rule"></div>
        <p class="poem">
          <span class="ln">A Bill from Billbrook, one fine day,</span>
          <span class="ln">Met Jurgen, who argued with famous debate;</span>
          <span class="ln">They argued for tea,</span>
          <span class="ln">Then the argument spilled into the sea,</span>
          <span class="ln">And Bill won it, shouting, “Yes, ja!”</span>
        </p>
        <div class="note"><b>Marginalia</b>Mr. Jürgen declines to comment. He will argue further.</div>
        <span class="stamp" aria-hidden="true">Read aloud</span>
      </article>

      <article class="lim rev" id="lim-5">
        <div class="lim-head"><span class="num">V</span><span class="place">The Bill of Billwick</span>
          <button class="recite" type="button" title="Recite, by highlighting, at a dignified pace">▸ Recite</button>
        </div>
        <div class="lim-rule"></div>
        <p class="poem">
          <span class="ln">There was a young Bill from Billwick,</span>
          <span class="ln">Who played cricket with a stick;</span>
          <span class="ln">He batted all day,</span>
          <span class="ln">Then he bowled anyway,</span>
          <span class="ln">And was out for a duck — what a trick!</span>
        </p>
        <div class="note"><b>Marginalia</b>The duck, on examination, was of exceptional thickness.</div>
        <span class="stamp" aria-hidden="true">Read aloud</span>
      </article>

      <article class="lim rev" id="lim-6">
        <div class="lim-head"><span class="num">VI</span><span class="place">The Old Bill &amp; the Brass Bell</span>
          <button class="recite" type="button" title="Recite, by highlighting, at a dignified pace">▸ Recite</button>
        </div>
        <div class="lim-rule"></div>
        <p class="poem">
          <span class="ln">There was an old Bill with a very big bell;</span>
          <span class="ln">He’d ring it at supper with all of his might;</span>
          <span class="ln">“Please!” called the street,</span>
          <span class="ln">“We are going to sleep!”</span>
          <span class="ln">But he’d ring, ring, ring, and feel very well.</span>
        </p>
        <div class="note"><b>Marginalia</b>The neighbours have since rehung their curtains and fled.</div>
        <span class="stamp" aria-hidden="true">Read aloud</span>
      </article>

      <article class="lim rev" id="lim-7">
        <div class="lim-head"><span class="num">VII</span><span class="place">The Bill of Billshire</span>
          <button class="recite" type="button" title="Recite, by highlighting, at a dignified pace">▸ Recite</button>
        </div>
        <div class="lim-rule"></div>
        <p class="poem">
          <span class="ln">There was a young Bill from Billshire,</span>
          <span class="ln">Who flew to the moon on a bicycle’s tire;</span>
          <span class="ln">He wheeled off the ground,</span>
          <span class="ln">Round the moon did he bound,</span>
          <span class="ln">And was back by the same breakfast, sir.</span>
        </p>
        <div class="note"><b>Marginalia</b>The bicycle has since been fitted with a small apology.</div>
        <span class="stamp" aria-hidden="true">Read aloud</span>
      </article>

      <article class="lim rev" id="lim-8">
        <div class="lim-head"><span class="num">VIII</span><span class="place">The Bill of Billfair</span>
          <button class="recite" type="button" title="Recite, by highlighting, at a dignified pace">▸ Recite</button>
        </div>
        <div class="lim-rule"></div>
        <p class="poem">
          <span class="ln">There once was a Bill from Billfair,</span>
          <span class="ln">Who forecasted rain from his parson’s chair;</span>
          <span class="ln">He’d consult with the cat,</span>
          <span class="ln">And the cat said, “That’s it!”</span>
          <span class="ln">And the heavens obliged without a care.</span>
        </p>
        <div class="note"><b>Marginalia</b>The cat’s methods have not been made available to the press.</div>
        <span class="stamp" aria-hidden="true">Read aloud</span>
      </article>

      <article class="lim rev" id="lim-9">
        <div class="lim-head"><span class="num">IX</span><span class="place">The Baker of the Hill</span>
          <button class="recite" type="button" title="Recite, by highlighting, at a dignified pace">▸ Recite</button>
        </div>
        <div class="lim-rule"></div>
        <p class="poem">
          <span class="ln">There once was a baker, dear Bill,</span>
          <span class="ln">Who’d knead up his dough with a double-arm drill;</span>
          <span class="ln">He whisked and he folded,</span>
          <span class="ln">He baked and he sold it,</span>
          <span class="ln">And his buns were renowned on the hill.</span>
        </p>
        <div class="note"><b>Marginalia</b>Buns, 2d. each. The hill, regretfully, unnamed.</div>
        <span class="stamp" aria-hidden="true">Read aloud</span>
      </article>

      <article class="lim rev" id="lim-10">
        <div class="lim-head"><span class="num">X</span><span class="place">The Sea-Bill of Billbay</span>
          <button class="recite" type="button" title="Recite, by highlighting, at a dignified pace">▸ Recite</button>
        </div>
        <div class="lim-rule"></div>
        <p class="poem">
          <span class="ln">There was a sea-Bill from Billbay,</span>
          <span class="ln">Who sailed through each storm on a Tuesday;</span>
          <span class="ln">The waves were quite high,</span>
          <span class="ln">And the gale did not lie,</span>
          <span class="ln">And he anchored at tea-time — hooray!</span>
        </p>
        <div class="note"><b>Marginalia</b>The Tuesday schedule was kept, to the crew’s surprise.</div>
        <span class="stamp" aria-hidden="true">Read aloud</span>
      </article>

      <article class="lim rev" id="lim-11">
        <div class="lim-head"><span class="num">XI</span><span class="place">The Bill Who Was Quick</span>
          <button class="recite" type="button" title="Recite, by highlighting, at a dignified pace">▸ Recite</button>
        </div>
        <div class="lim-rule"></div>
        <p class="poem">
          <span class="ln">There once was a Bill who was nimble and quick,</span>
          <span class="ln">Who’d vanish a rabbit and call it a trick;</span>
          <span class="ln">He’d pull from a hat,</span>
          <span class="ln">And the rabbit sat flat,</span>
          <span class="ln">Then vanished — the trick! — and the rabbit went sick.</span>
        </p>
        <div class="note"><b>Marginalia</b>The rabbit was, by its own account, unwell for some weeks.</div>
        <span class="stamp" aria-hidden="true">Read aloud</span>
      </article>

      <article class="lim rev" id="lim-12">
        <div class="lim-head"><span class="num">XII</span><span class="place">The Bill of Billdown</span>
          <button class="recite" type="button" title="Recite, by highlighting, at a dignified pace">▸ Recite</button>
        </div>
        <div class="lim-rule"></div>
        <p class="poem">
          <span class="ln">There was a young Bill from Billdown,</span>
          <span class="ln">Who grew cabbages bigger than houses in town;</span>
          <span class="ln">He’d water and weed,</span>
          <span class="ln">And the cabbages would breed,</span>
          <span class="ln">Till the harvest came down — and the neighbours did frown.</span>
        </p>
        <div class="note"><b>Marginalia</b>The vicar’s frown lasted until the next planting season.</div>
        <span class="stamp" aria-hidden="true">Read aloud</span>
      </article>

      <article class="lim rev" id="lim-13">
        <div class="lim-head"><span class="num">XIII</span><span class="place">The Dentist of the Drill</span>
          <button class="recite" type="button" title="Recite, by highlighting, at a dignified pace">▸ Recite</button>
        </div>
        <div class="lim-rule"></div>
        <p class="poem">
          <span class="ln">There was a young Bill at the dentist, dear Bill,</span>
          <span class="ln">Who’d sing “Pop Goes the Weasel” on every drill;</span>
          <span class="ln">The patient said, “Please!”</span>
          <span class="ln">But he sang with great ease,</span>
          <span class="ln">And the patient said, “Doctor — what a thrill!”</span>
        </p>
        <div class="note"><b>Marginalia</b>“Pop Goes the Weasel” was sung in B-flat, at full volume.</div>
        <span class="stamp" aria-hidden="true">Read aloud</span>
      </article>

      <article class="lim rev" id="lim-14">
        <div class="lim-head"><span class="num">XIV</span><span class="place">The Bill of the Chessboard</span>
          <button class="recite" type="button" title="Recite, by highlighting, at a dignified pace">▸ Recite</button>
        </div>
        <div class="lim-rule"></div>
        <p class="poem">
          <span class="ln">There once was a Bill who would play at his chess,</span>
          <span class="ln">He’d checkmate in four moves or less;</span>
          <span class="ln">His opponents would weep:</span>
          <span class="ln">“There is no way to keep</span>
          <span class="ln">A knight from dear Bill.” The grandmaster sighed, “He is best in the class.”</span>
        </p>
        <div class="note"><b>Marginalia</b>The grandmaster is now playing for the second table, quietly.</div>
        <span class="stamp" aria-hidden="true">Read aloud</span>
      </article>

      <article class="lim rev" id="lim-15">
        <div class="lim-head"><span class="num">XV</span><span class="place">The Mail-Bill of Bill’s End</span>
          <button class="recite" type="button" title="Recite, by highlighting, at a dignified pace">▸ Recite</button>
        </div>
        <div class="lim-rule"></div>
        <p class="poem">
          <span class="ln">There was a mail-Bill at Bill’s End;</span>
          <span class="ln">The letters all came; the whole town was his friend;</span>
          <span class="ln">He’d knock, then he’d bang,</span>
          <span class="ln">“The mail for the gang!”</span>
          <span class="ln">And the last letter always landed back at Bill’s End.</span>
        </p>
        <div class="note"><b>Marginalia</b>No letter, however large, was ever known to be lost.</div>
        <span class="stamp" aria-hidden="true">Read aloud</span>
      </article>

      <article class="lim rev" id="lim-16">
        <div class="lim-head"><span class="num">XVI</span><span class="place">The Bill Who Wrote These</span>
          <button class="recite" type="button" title="Recite, by highlighting, at a dignified pace">▸ Recite</button>
        </div>
        <div class="lim-rule"></div>
        <p class="poem">
          <span class="ln">There was a young Bill who wrote limericks quick,</span>
          <span class="ln">One a minute, no less — every one a trick;</span>
          <span class="ln">He’d rhyme town with frown,</span>
          <span class="ln">And he’d rhyme Bill with June,</span>
          <span class="ln">And the twenty-fifth — this one — he wrote quick.</span>
        </p>
        <div class="note"><b>Marginalia</b>The reviewer declines to disclose which method he used.</div>
        <span class="stamp" aria-hidden="true">Read aloud</span>
      </article>

      <article class="lim rev" id="lim-17">
        <div class="lim-head"><span class="num">XVII</span><span class="place">The Bill of the Golden Kazoo</span>
          <button class="recite" type="button" title="Recite, by highlighting, at a dignified pace">▸ Recite</button>
        </div>
        <div class="lim-rule"></div>
        <p class="poem">
          <span class="ln">There once was a Bill with a golden kazoo,</span>
          <span class="ln">Who played at the wedding and the funeral too;</span>
          <span class="ln">He played in the park,</span>
          <span class="ln">He played at the dark,</span>
          <span class="ln">And the vicar joined in: “Doo, doo, doo, doo!”</span>
        </p>
        <div class="note"><b>Marginalia</b>The vicar’s part was in C major; the dogs were in tune.</div>
        <span class="stamp" aria-hidden="true">Read aloud</span>
      </article>

      <article class="lim rev" id="lim-18">
        <div class="lim-head"><span class="num">XVIII</span><span class="place">The Bill of Forty-Seven Cats</span>
          <button class="recite" type="button" title="Recite, by highlighting, at a dignified pace">▸ Recite</button>
        </div>
        <div class="lim-rule"></div>
        <p class="poem">
          <span class="ln">There once was a Bill with a thousand cat names,</span>
          <span class="ln">From “Biscuit” to “Bilberry” to “The Duke’s Old James”;</span>
          <span class="ln">He’d whistle and call,</span>
          <span class="ln">And they answered, one and all,</span>
          <span class="ln">And all forty-seven purred at the same.</span>
        </p>
        <div class="note"><b>Marginalia</b>Forty-seven, to be precise. The forty-eighth was a dog.</div>
        <span class="stamp" aria-hidden="true">Read aloud</span>
      </article>

      <article class="lim rev" id="lim-19">
        <div class="lim-head"><span class="num">XIX</span><span class="place">The Librarian of the Shush</span>
          <button class="recite" type="button" title="Recite, by highlighting, at a dignified pace">▸ Recite</button>
        </div>
        <div class="lim-rule"></div>
        <p class="poem">
          <span class="ln">There once was a Bill whose shush was a violence;</span>
          <span class="ln">He’d hush up a giggle with quiet insistence;</span>
          <span class="ln">A pin could be heard,</span>
          <span class="ln">A bird could be blurred,</span>
          <span class="ln">But the loudest sound in the room — his silence.</span>
        </p>
        <div class="note"><b>Marginalia</b>A pin, dropped at 3 p.m., was heard in full court at 3:04.</div>
        <span class="stamp" aria-hidden="true">Read aloud</span>
      </article>

      <article class="lim rev" id="lim-20">
        <div class="lim-head"><span class="num">XX</span><span class="place">The Soccer-Bill of the Left Boot</span>
          <button class="recite" type="button" title="Recite, by highlighting, at a dignified pace">▸ Recite</button>
        </div>
        <div class="lim-rule"></div>
        <p class="poem">
