The page opens as a printed broadside — "The Billian Almanack" — complete with bunting, a rotating seal, and a dotted-leader contents page, then settles into a two-column catalogue of all 25 numbered limericks (each with its own marginal note and a "recite" button that carries the eye down the five lines). Verse III features the economist who never could read his own bill, and Verse IV the Bill of Billbrook who argued with a certain Jurgen right into the sea. A settled ledger, a price list, and a working order form ("one bill enclosed") round out the accounts.

