        </div>
        <div class="lim-rule"></div>
        <p class="poem">
          <span class="ln">There once was a Bill with a golden kazoo,</span>
          <span class="ln">Who played at the wedding and the funeral too;</span>
          <span class="ln">He played in the park,</span>
          <span class="ln">He played at the dark,</span>
          <span class="ln">And the vicar joined in: “Doo, doo, doo, doo!”</span>
        </p>
        <div class="note"><b>Marginalia</b>The vicar’s part was in C major; the dogs were in tune.</div>
        <span class="stamp" aria-hidden="true">Read aloud</span>
      </article>

      <article class="lim rev" id="lim-18">
        <div class="lim-head"><span class="num">XVIII</span><span class="place">The Bill of Forty-Seven Cats</span>
          <button class="recite" type="button" title="Recite, by highlighting, at a dignified pace">▸ Recite</button>
        </div>
        <div class="lim-rule"></div>
        <p class="poem">
          <span class="ln">There once was a Bill with a thousand cat names,</span>
          <span class="ln">From “Biscuit” to “Bilberry” to “The Duke’s Old James”;</span>
          <span class="ln">He’d whistle and call,</span>
          <span class="ln">And they answered, one and all,</span>
          <span class="ln">And all forty-seven purred at the same.</span>
        </p>
        <div class="note"><b>Marginalia</b>Forty-seven, to be precise. The forty-eighth was a dog.</div>
        <span class="stamp" aria-hidden="true">Read aloud</span>
      </article>

      <article class="lim rev" id="lim-19">
        <div class="lim-head"><span class="num">XIX</span><span class="place">The Librarian of the Shush</span>
