        </div>
        <div class="lim-rule"></div>
        <p class="poem">
          <span class="ln">There once was a chef in the village, dear Bill,</span>
          <span class="ln">Who’d cook up a soufflé that rose over the hill;</span>
          <span class="ln">It rose, then it fell,</span>
          <span class="ln">We cleaned up the smell,</span>
          <span class="ln">But the critics said, “Worth every spill.”</span>
        </p>
        <div class="note"><b>Marginalia</b>The soufflé reached the hill. The hill declined to comment.</div>
        <span class="stamp" aria-hidden="true">Read aloud</span>
      </article>

      <article class="lim rev" id="lim-22">
        <div class="lim-head"><span class="num">XXII</span><span class="place">The Bill of the Telescope</span>
          <button class="recite" type="button" title="Recite, by highlighting, at a dignified pace">▸ Recite</button>
        </div>
        <div class="lim-rule"></div>
        <p class="poem">
          <span class="ln">There once was a Bill in his tent one bright night,</span>
          <span class="ln">Who was searching for Pluto with telescope’s sight;</span>
          <span class="ln">He squinted, he counted,</span>
          <span class="ln">Till the telescope dented,</span>
          <span class="ln">Then he wrote, “Star 9,412: a dim light.”</span>
        </p>
        <div class="note"><b>Marginalia</b>Star 9,412 has been reclassified: “A Dim Light, Allegedly.”</div>
        <span class="stamp" aria-hidden="true">Read aloud</span>
      </article>

      <article class="lim rev" id="lim-23">
        <div class="lim-head"><span class="num">XXIII</span><span class="place">The Engineer of the Main Line</span>
          <button class="recite" type="button" title="Recite, by highlighting, at a dignified pace">▸ Recite</button>
        </div>
        <div class="lim-rule"></div>
        <p class="poem">
          <span class="ln">There once was a Bill who drove engines on the main line,</span>
          <span class="ln">His whistle sang “Row, Row, Row Your Boat,” in time;</span>
          <span class="ln">The passengers cheered,</span>
          <span class="ln">The signalman sneered,</span>
          <span class="ln">All off at the dot, in fine time.</span>
        </p>
        <div class="note"><b>Marginalia</b>The signalman is still unimpressed, but punctually.</div>
        <span class="stamp" aria-hidden="true">Read aloud</span>
      </article>

      <article class="lim rev" id="lim-24">
        <div class="lim-head"><span class="num">XXIV</span><span class="place">The Bill the Peer</span>
          <button class="recite" type="button" title="Recite, by highlighting, at a dignified pace">▸ Recite</button>
        </div>
        <div class="lim-rule"></div>
        <p class="poem">
          <span class="ln">There once was a Bill, a young knight-errant and peer,</span>
          <span class="ln">Whose lance was a broom and whose shield was a pear;</span>
          <span class="ln">He’d tilt for an hour,</span>
          <span class="ln">In a castle’s own tower,</span>
          <span class="ln">Till the dragon surrendered: “You’re too keen, dear!”</span>
        </p>
        <div class="note"><b>Marginalia</b>The pear has been preserved in the castle cellar.</div>
        <span class="stamp" aria-hidden="true">Read aloud</span>
      </article>

      <article class="lim rev" id="lim-25">
        <div class="lim-head"><span class="num">XXV</span><span class="place">A Toast to the Twenty-Sixth</span>
          <button class="recite" type="button" title="Recite, by highlighting, at a dignified pace">▸ Recite</button>
        </div>
        <div class="lim-rule"></div>
        <p class="poem">
          <span class="ln">So here’s to all Bills, one and all,</span>
          <span class="ln">From Billhaven’s quay to Billshire’s call;</span>
          <span class="ln">May your limericks rhyme,</span>
          <span class="ln">May your teapots always chime,</span>
          <span class="ln">And the twenty-sixth Bill will outdo them all.</span>
        </p>
        <div class="note"><b>Marginalia</b>The twenty-sixth Bill is being consulted. He is not pleased.</div>
        <span class="stamp" aria-hidden="true">Read aloud</span>
      </article>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

